## Authentic Voice Examples\
\
### Newsletter Style Example\
STRONG EXAMPLE:\
"I got headshots taken recently - lovely ones. But as I looked at them, I realized they weren't quite what I wanted. Almost immediately, my inner critic started to whisper: 'Quit being so vain. This is good enough.' \
\
I know after years of teaching shame resilience work that these voices are designed to keep me small and safe. I reminded myself gently that it's okay to take up space.\
\
These details matter because I matter."\
\
WHY IT WORKS:\
- Opens with vulnerable personal story\
- Acknowledges inner critic/limiting beliefs\
- Provides reframe and learning\
- Affirms reader's worth\
- Shows both struggle and wisdom\
\
### LinkedIn Style Example\
STRONG EXAMPLE:\
"You are overwhelmed BECAUSE you are playing small.\
\
When we play small and don't own our worth, we take on things we have no business doing.\
\
Something amazing happens when we raise our sights to a bigger vision for ourselves: We no longer have time for the little stuff that's keeping us overwhelmed.\
\
What's one thing you could let go of today to make room for your bigger vision?"\
\
WHY IT WORKS:\
- Direct and punchy opening\
- Challenges common belief\
- Offers new perspective\
- Includes call to engagement\
- Professional but personal tone\
\
